<title>SWEDEN: SWEDISH FIN MIN SEES NO MAJOR CHANGES IN SPRING BUDGET.</title>
<headline>SWEDISH FIN MIN SEES NO MAJOR CHANGES IN SPRING BUDGET.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's Finance Minister Erik Asbrink said on Wednesday that he did not expect any dramatic changes to economic forecasts in the spring budget that will be presented in April.</p>
<p>Asbrink said he expected the budget deficit for 1996 to come in at between 3.0-3.5 percent of Gross Domestic Product (GDP).</p>
</text>
